IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-wc-core`

-- Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW), with the 1998 Act and the 2016 Regulation -- from the seat of the employer.
--
-- SEAT: the employer of the injured worker, insured with a licensed insurer or the Nominal Insurer, or itself a
-- self-insurer. The 1998 Act and the Regulation put real duties on it, each with a deadline or a penalty: notify the
-- insurer within 48 hours of becoming aware of a workplace injury (s 44(2); Regulation cl 36), forward a claim within 7
-- days (s 264(1)), give requested information within 7 days (s 264(2)), provide suitable work at the worker's request
-- (s 49), and keep the notification records for 5 years and produce them within 7 days of a request (Regulation cl 35).
-- "What must I do, by when, and what follows if I don't?" The rules are in nsw-wc-core.l4; this module restates none, and
-- keeps its own names (none shared with nsw-wc-seat.l4 or nsw-wc-seat-insurer.l4).
--
-- Edition: the Open Australian Legal Corpus texts as at 10 March 2025 -- not the current official text, and possibly out
-- of date. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW) -- the employer's questions`

§§ `When a worker is injured (1998 Act s 44; Regulation cl 35)`

@export Within how many hours of becoming aware of a workplace injury must I notify my insurer (1998 Act s 44(2), (4))? No answer means no duty, as a self-insurer.
GIVEN `I am a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a licensed self-insurer
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Within how many hours must I notify my insurer` MEANS
    `the hours to notify the insurer, if any` `I am a self-insurer`

@export Did I notify my insurer of the workplace injury in time (1998 Act s 44(2))?
GIVEN `I am a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a licensed self-insurer
      `the hours from becoming aware to notifying` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours passed between your becoming aware that the worker had received a workplace injury and your notifying the insurer or the Nominal Insurer (electronically, on the approved form, or by telephone: Regulation cl 35(1))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I notify my insurer in time` IF
    CONSIDER `the hours to notify the insurer, if any` `I am a self-insurer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST `the hours allowed` THEN `the hours from becoming aware to notifying` AT MOST `the hours allowed`

@export Until when must I keep my records of the injury notification (Regulation cl 35(2))?
GIVEN `the day I notified the insurer` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the s 44(2) notification (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when must I keep my notification records` MEANS
    `the records must be kept until at least` `the day I notified the insurer`

@export By what day must I make my notification records available after a request (Regulation cl 35(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE @desc The day an inspector or an authorised employee representative asked to inspect the records (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I make my notification records available` MEANS
    `days after` `the days to make the notification records available (Regulation cl 35(3))` `the day of the request`

§§ `When I receive a claim, or the insurer asks for information (1998 Act s 264)`

@export By what day must I forward this claim to my insurer (1998 Act s 264(1))? No answer means no duty, as a self-insurer.
GIVEN `I am a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a licensed self-insurer
      `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim or the document about it (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By what day must I forward the claim` MEANS
    `the day to forward the claim by, if any` `I am a self-insurer` `the day I received the claim`

@export By what day must I give my insurer the information or documents it asked for about a claim or notified injury (1998 Act s 264(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the insurer's request` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the insurer's request (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I give the insurer what it asked for` MEANS
    `days after` `the days to give requested information (1998 Act s 264(2))` `the day I received the insurer's request`

§§ `When the worker can return to work (1998 Act s 49)`

-- Situation: the injured worker is able to do some work.
@export Must I provide suitable work for this injured worker (1998 Act s 49)?
GIVEN `the worker can return to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is able to return to work, full-time or part-time, in the old job or another
      `the worker has asked me for suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has asked you to provide suitable employment
      `it is not reasonably practicable for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not reasonably practicable for you to provide suitable employment
      `the worker left voluntarily after the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker voluntarily left your employment after the injury
      `I ended the worker's employment after the injury, not for unfitness from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you terminated the worker's employment after the injury for a reason other than the worker's unfitness from the injury
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I provide suitable work` IF
    `the employer must provide suitable employment`
        (`Suitable work facts` WITH
            `the worker is able to return to work`                                         IS `the worker can return to work`
            `the worker has asked the employer for suitable employment`                     IS `the worker has asked me for suitable work`
            `it is not reasonably practicable to provide it`                               IS `it is not reasonably practicable for me`
            `the worker voluntarily left the employment after the injury`                  IS `the worker left voluntarily after the injury`
            `the employer ended the employment after the injury, not for unfitness from the injury` IS `I ended the worker's employment after the injury, not for unfitness from it`)

§§ `What follows if I miss a duty`

@export What follows if I, the employer, miss this duty: the maximum penalty, the penalty notice amount, and other consequences?
GIVEN `the employer's duty` IS A `Duty` @desc The duty: s 44(2) notifying the insurer, s 264(1) forwarding a claim, s 264(2) giving information, s 49 suitable work, or Regulation cl 35(3) records
GIVETH A `Consequence`
`What follows if I, the employer, miss this duty` MEANS
    `the consequence of missing` `the employer's duty`
